  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14251762/assets/b3fcbed98f7838b4885e2ca14cb1192c039e0b1d35e5980cca363ec4cdc6f9f5.png)\n\nThe function $w(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-6,3].$ The graph of ${w}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $w(x),$ is shown above, where the areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $7,$ $5,$ and $1$ respectively (from left to right). Find the maximum value of $w(x)$ on the interval $[-6,3]$ given that $w(-6)=-4.$\n\n${w}_{\\text{max}}=$\n{{field-1}}",
